1 FACT Samuel Still II fought in the Revolutionary War .  He sided with England.  In 1780-1781 his commanding officer's friend, who was an American patriot, was imprisoned on a prison ship in Wilmington, NC.  Samuel and his officer visited the prison ship and gained the release of the patriot.  Later, the patriot's men fought and killed Samuel and his officer.  They were then hung/tied to a tree and left in view to discourage further fighting.
2 TYPE Life sketch
