1 EVEN 16925967
2 TYPE Find a Grave Memorial %23
1 EVEN About 40 to 50 Indians killed James and his whole family, 11 in number.  They burned the  house and fencing and carried off all his stock..  When the soldiers came they wrapped James in a sheet and buried him where a tree had uprooted, not having tools for digging a proper grave.  The soldiers found the remains of two of his childfen and buried them beside him.  His wife Martha and daughter Jane who were captured were taken to Chilicothe, Ohio and burned at the stake.  William, Alexander, Margaret, John and infant children were massacred.  James and Mary Moore, son and daughter and Martha Evans, who were captured were carried to Canada, held captive for 5 years, were rescued by Thomas Evans, brother of Martha Evans. Also, William McPhaetus of Staunton was james and Martha Evan's uncle who lived near the Middle River. Thomas found them near Detroit. He was paid out of the Moore's estate
