1 FACT Elisha Noah Clayton's twin brother is Elijah Clayton.  Burial place is now listed as in West Virginia not Virginia since West Virginia broke off from the state of Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisha Clayton served more than 3 years of active service in the American Revolutionary War between 1776 and 1781.  He married Elizabeth King in Delaware.  Then he married Elizabeth Little on 15 October 1793 after his first wife died.  He enlisted in the Monmouth County, New Jersey regiment with his brother Elijah.  He served under Captain J. Smook in Colonel herd's New Jersey regiment.  He took part at  fighting in Long Island and Monmouth, and was captured and held prisoner for 9 months in New York.
2 TYPE Life sketch
