1 FACT Catherine Sherrerd Piatt McHenry (1746-1827) was born on 11 Nov 1746 in Culpeper, Culpeper Co, Virginia and died on 22 May 1827 in Warren Co, New Jersey. She was the daughter of Thomas Sherrard (an Irishman) and Catherine Andriesen (an American). Catherine married Daniel Piatt and settled in Pluckemin, NJ where their 7 children were born. Daniel was a Captain and Major in the American Revolutionary War and died of pneumonia contracted on a mission during the war in the frigid winter (April 1780). Daniel & Catherine had 7 children ages 4 to 14, Catherine married Charles McHenry after the death of her husband.
2 CONT She was a member of the Presbyterian Church of Mansfield and is buried in their cemetery, Mansfield Woodhouse Cemetery. There is a transcription of her headstone at http://raub-and-more.com/mansfieldcem2.html but Michael Holmes could not find it when he went to take a picture so it may be illegible, broken, fallen or gone.
2 CONT Catherine is my 4th great grandmother.
